<section class="panel">
  <div class="panel-head">
    <p class="panel-kicker">Runtime contract</p>
    <h2>Host → seam → Zig</h2>
    <p class="panel-copy">
      Astro is chrome, not the runtime. <code>@zt-ui/stage</code> is the portable seam — input in, command buffers out, Canvas2D paint. Same mount from Next or vanilla.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="contract-list">
    <div>
      <strong>Lifecycle</strong>
      <p><code>initRuntime</code>, <code>resize</code>, <code>beginFrame</code></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Input</strong>
      <p><code>pointerMove</code>, <code>pointerButton</code>, <code>pointerWheel</code>, <code>keyEvent</code></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Buffers</strong>
      <p><code>getCommandsPtr/Len</code>, <code>getTextPtr/Len</code>, <code>getPointsPtr/Len</code>, <code>memory</code></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Stage seam</strong>
      <p><code>web-stage/</code> · <code>@zt-ui/stage</code> — mount, input fan-in, Canvas2D hot path. Framework-agnostic by design.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Optional shell snapshot</strong>
      <p><code>getSnapshotPtr/Len</code> when chrome needs a low-frequency mirror of Zig state.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
